; This year's journal. Use this file day to day: specify it with hledger's -f option or $LEDGER_FILE.
; For reports across several years, use all.journal.
; To start a new year, make a new YEAR.journal like this one, with that year's opening balances
; (https://hledger.org/hledger.html#close can generate them).
; Syntax: https://hledger.org/hledger.html#journal

; Declarations, helpful for reports and error checking,
; shared by all years and kept in their own files for easier maintenance.

include accounts.journal
include commodities.journal
include payees.journal


; Opening balances.
; Record the balances of the assets and liabilities to be tracked, at the start of the year
; (or at a later start date, in your first year).
; The clopen tag helps hledger close generate next year's opening balances.

2026-01-01 opening balances
    ; clopen:2026
    assets:bank:checking                       $1000
    assets:cash                                 $100
    liabilities:bank:credit card                $-50.12
    equity:start

; Transactions.
; Keeping them in date order allows extra error checking (hledger check ordereddates).

2026-01-02 received wages
    revenues:salary
    assets:bank:checking                       $1000

2026-01-03 Whole Foods | bought groceries
    assets:cash
    expenses:food                                $50

